{"nodes": [{"id": "src_chrono_fsi_sph_cmakelists_chrono_fsisph", "label": "Chrono_fsisph Library Target", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "src/chrono_fsi/sph/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_chrono_fsi_sph_cmakelists_chrono_fsisph_vsg", "label": "Chrono_fsisph_vsg Visualization Target", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "src/chrono_fsi/sph/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Under HIP its visualization source is compiled with LANGUAGE HIP because it includes FSI data-manager headers referencing rocThrust/rocPRIM device types that do not compile as plain C++."}, {"id": "src_chrono_fsi_sph_cmakelists_thrust_device_system_wiring", "label": "SPH Thrust Device-System Wiring", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_fsi/sph/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Thrust's device system follows the HIP PLATFORM, not merely the fact that the backend is HIP: THRUST_DEVICE_SYSTEM_HIP means rocThrust, which exists only in ROCm, so when HIP targets NVIDIA the correct system is CUDA. Computed once at submodule scope because Chrono_fsisph and the VSG plugin must agree, and letting the plugin decide separately is exactly how it went out of step. The definitions stay PRIVATE and nothing is exported: no installed header includes <thrust/...>, exporting THRUST_DEVICE_SYSTEM_CUDA collided with Chrono::Multicore's THRUST_DEVICE_SYSTEM_OMP (last one silently winning, macro-redefinition warnings on vehicle demos), and exporting _CPP would silently demote a consumer's own device Thrust - Chrono::Sensor calls thrust::device_vector on CUDA device pointers and would segfault at runtime rather than fail to build."}, {"id": "src_chrono_fsi_sph_cmakelists_fsisph_gpu_visibility", "label": "Asymmetric GPU Runtime Visibility", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_fsi/sph/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "CUDA is PUBLIC because public headers switch on CHRONO_USE_CUDA and then include <cuda_runtime.h>, so consumers inheriting the definition must also inherit CUDA include directories from CUDA::cudart_static (a public definition with a private link breaks every downstream target, Chrono_parsers first). HIP is PRIVATE because public consumers are ordinary C++ TUs and the HIP target's definitions would force Thrust onto rocPRIM in code that never asked for it."}, {"id": "src_chrono_fsi_sph_cmakelists_splashsurf", "label": "Splashsurf Surface Reconstruction", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "src/chrono_fsi/sph/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Optional external executable; when absent the surface reconstruction utility is compiled out via CHRONO_HAS_SPLASHSURF."}], "edges": [{"source": "src_chrono_fsi_sph_cmakelists_chrono_fsisph", "target": "src_chrono_fsi_cmakelists_chrono_fsi", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "src/chrono_fsi/sph/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "src_chrono_fsi_sph_cmakelists_chrono_fsisph", "target": "src_chrono_cmakelists_chrono_core", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "src/chrono_fsi/sph/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "src_chrono_fsi_sph_cmakelists_chrono_fsisph_vsg", "target": "src_chrono_fsi_sph_cmakelists_chrono_fsisph", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "src/chrono_fsi/sph/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "src_chrono_fsi_sph_cmake